---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.1 · Slayer Foundation & While Guthix Sleeps" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-1" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Slayer Foundation &amp; While Guthix Sleeps</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Open the pirate/Mos Le'Harmless route, use quest rewards before training Slayer, close The Path of Glouphrie, hit the small Magic-67 WGS gate, and finish While Guthix Sleeps without overtraining combat or camping an RNG item.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Rum Deal → Cabin Fever → Great Brain Robbery → actual 56 Slayer and 60 Strength → Path of Glouphrie → actual 58 Slayer → actual 67 Magic → While Guthix Sleeps."
        stats={["Read live XP at every gate; quest lamps land before the next training block", "Actual 60 Strength, 58 Slayer and 67 Magic by the WGS finale", "Black mask and every other RNG upgrade remain optional"]}
        unlocks={["Holy wrench and Mos Le'Harmless/Cave Horror access", "Poison Waste Dungeon and its spirit-tree destination", "Ancient Guthixian Temple and normal Tormented Demons after WGS"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>The Chapter 3 contract:</strong> this is not BRUHsailer's maxing home stretch. The linear graduation target is every currently released quest, Fire Cape and reliable transport, supplies and combat infrastructure—with enough real boss experience to choose your own endgame afterward. Bowfa/crystal, raids, gear hunts, diaries, Combat Achievements, collection log, relaxed progression and eventual 99s are optional Endgame Paths. <strong>Optional RNG items never block the Quest Cape / Fire Cape progress meter.</strong> You do not need an Enhanced Crystal Weapon Seed to finish this guide.</div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Chapter 2 handoff audit—information, not a progress box.</strong> Check the live skill tab and bank: Chapter 2 guarantees approximately actual <strong>51+ Slayer, 66+ Magic, 60+ Attack</strong>, Attack + Strength ≥130, 70 Prayer and Defence, Piety, dragon defender, Barrows gloves, Helm of Neitiznot, Proselyte, upgraded Iban's staff, 70+ Herblore and 72+ Thieving. It also covered the other WGS skill gates. <strong>Actual 60 Strength still needs its own check</strong>; the Attack + Strength total alone does not prove it. Do not project Hitpoints or combat levels from a sample account. If a claimed prior mandatory unlock is missing, repair that checkpoint before treating it as guaranteed here.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Pirate chain · useful rewards first</div><h2>Three quests before the measured Slayer work.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-rum-deal" number="1" title="Complete Rum Deal; keep the Holy wrench">
        <p><strong>Why now:</strong> Rum Deal starts the pirate chain for Cabin Fever, pays <strong>7,000 XP each in Prayer, Farming and Fishing</strong>, and awards the Holy wrench. The route already has Zogre Flesh Eaters, Priest in Peril, actual 42 Slayer, 42 Crafting, 40 Farming, 47 Prayer and 50 Fishing. Begin with <strong>Pirate Pete at the dock north-east of the Ectofuntus</strong>; the Ectophial makes the approach easy. Bring ordinary combat gear, food, a teleport and a way to attack from a distance for the level-150 Evil spirit and diseased fever spider. A rake, seed dibber and bucket can be obtained during the quest, but taking yours avoids an extra search. Have at least 47 current Prayer points when Davey blesses the wrench. Protect from Melee or safespot the Evil spirit; use distance or disease treatment for the spider. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rum_Deal" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest details</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Retain the Holy wrench.</strong> In your inventory it improves Prayer-potion restoration; bank it when the inventory slot matters more. There is no requirement to carry it constantly.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-cabin-fever" number="2" title="Complete Cabin Fever; open Mos Le'Harmless">
        <p>Continue to <strong>Bill Teach at The Green Ghost inn in Port Phasmatys</strong>. Pirate's Treasure, Rum Deal, Big Chompy Bird Hunting, Zogre Flesh Eaters, Jungle Potion, Druidic Ritual and Priest in Peril are already complete; actual 42 Agility, 45 Crafting, 50 Smithing and 40 Ranged are covered. The quest needs <strong>no complicated external item list</strong>: leave roughly 11 free inventory spaces, bring ordinary food/gear for level-57 pirates and follow the ship's tasks. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Cabin_Fever" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
        <p>The payoff is <strong>Mos Le'Harmless and access to its Cave Horror cave</strong>, which makes the later black-mask option possible. The charter-ship discount and Trouble Brewing access are bonuses, not new errands. You can return by speaking to Bill Teach at Port Phasmatys; the Ectophial is a convenient return leg.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-brain-robbery" number="3" title="Complete The Great Brain Robbery; put its 5,000-XP lamp into Slayer">
        <p>Start with <strong>Brother Tranquility on Mos Le'Harmless</strong>. Creature of Fenkenstrain, Cabin Fever and Recipe for Disaster's Pirate Pete subquest are complete; actual 50 Prayer and the Crafting/Construction gates are covered. Before the relevant phase, bank-check <strong>fishbowl helmet plus diving apparatus</strong> (or a medallion of the deep), <strong>ring of charos</strong>, holy symbol, hammer, about 100 nails and <strong>18 normal planks</strong> if you must make the ten wooden cats yourself. The cats also take <strong>ten ordinary furs</strong> at a POH Workshop clockmaker's bench; if that bench is absent, add <strong>four oak planks and a saw</strong> to build it. The 18 normal planks cover ten cats plus the quest's eight other planks; do not carry them all through every trip. Reclaim missing diving gear from Murphy at Port Khazard or the ring from Fenkenstrain as the quest allows. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Great_Brain_Robbery/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current item and phase checklist</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Barrelchest warning:</strong> the level-190 fight can drain and switch off Prayer, so do not assume uninterrupted Protect from Melee. Bring several Prayer potions, roughly ten good food and a ranged/Magic setup if you want the current entrance/corner safespot; do <em>not</em> hide directly behind a pew, where the anchor's ground strike can still hit. It is not undead, so Salve is no help. If you die, reclaiming items may require another underwater set; plan that before a second attempt. The anchor is a reward, <strong>not a mandatory weapon upgrade</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Great_Brain_Robbery" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fight and reward reference</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the direct <strong>6,000 Prayer, 3,000 Crafting and 2,000 Construction XP</strong>. Use the selectable <strong>5,000-XP blessed lamp on Slayer immediately</strong>, then read live Slayer XP for the next step. This lamp helps the imminent hard gate; Herblore already clears the core quest requirements.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Slayer · first live checkpoint</div><h2>Train the remainder, not the whole inherited grind.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-slayer-56" number="4" title="Reach actual 56 Slayer and verify actual 60 Strength">
        <p>After the Brain Robbery lamp, read your <strong>live Slayer XP</strong> and do only the remaining tasks to actual <strong>56 Slayer</strong>. At the same time, inspect actual Strength. If below <strong>60 Strength</strong>, put your dragon scimitar on an aggressive/Strength style during ordinary Slayer tasks. If Slayer reaches 56 first and Strength is somehow still short, finish only that Strength remainder; do not create a separate crab grind up front. These are Path's unboosted gates, not estimates from combat level.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i31-slayer-methods" skill="Slayer" target="actual 56 + Strength 60" why="Path consumes both live gates; quest XP arrives next." recommended="Nieve, if your live combat level is at least 85: take normal assignments and train combat naturally." relaxed="Another appropriate Slayer master is fine if you prefer their tasks; finish ordinary assignments at your own pace." informational={true} />
        <p><strong>First-timer loop:</strong> Nieve stands by the Stronghold Slayer Cave and southern bank in the <strong>Tree Gnome Stronghold</strong>; use the spirit tree to the Stronghold and run south-west. She requires <strong>85 combat</strong>, which the mandatory route should clear, but check your live combat level; if not, use an eligible master such as Chaeldar. Ask for a task, bring its required Slayer equipment, kill the assigned monsters and return for the next task. No block-list project, point-boosting rota, cannon, barrage, task spreadsheet or mandatory task bracelets is assumed. <strong>Stop at actual 56;</strong> do not train toward 58 yet, because Path's fixed Slayer XP comes first. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nieve" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nieve access</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-path" number="5" title="Complete The Path of Glouphrie and claim all four fixed XP lamps">
        <p><strong>Hard-stop preflight:</strong> actual <strong>56 Slayer, 60 Strength, 56 Thieving, 47 Ranged and 45 Agility</strong>, plus The Eyes of Glouphrie, Waterfall Quest and Tree Gnome Village. The last three skills/quests are Chapter 2 guarantees; the Slayer and Strength checks are why Step 4 exists. Begin with <strong>King Bolren in Tree Gnome Village</strong>. Use the spirit tree/gnome network for early stages, then <strong>fairy ring BKP</strong> and run north-west toward Longramble in the Galarpos Mountains. Bring food, combat gear, a crossbow and mith grapple for the crossing; keep the quest's crystal chime for the warped enemies in the Poison Waste Dungeon. Quest Helper can handle the coloured-shape puzzles. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Path_of_Glouphrie" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest and requirement reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>If no mith grapple is banked:</strong> at an anvil, use a hammer and <strong>one mithril bar</strong> to smith a mith grapple tip (59 Smithing; no mould). Attach the tip to <strong>one mithril bolt</strong> at 59 Fletching, then add <strong>one rope</strong>. The Chapter 2 route clears both skills. Equip the grapple as ammunition and a crossbow in the weapon slot for the crossing; do not assume an old diary grapple survived. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mith_grapple" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Grapple recipe</a>.</p>
        <p>At the dungeon, use the crystal chime as directed against warped terrorbirds; take food and Protect from Missiles, and use the rooms/doorways to isolate the final group if needed. Finish the quest and <strong>use all four fixed lamps now:</strong> <strong>20,000 Slayer, 30,000 Strength, 5,000 Magic and 5,000 Thieving XP</strong>. These rewards are lamps to claim, not automatic XP to assume. Path completes a major WGS prerequisite and opens the <strong>Poison Waste Dungeon and a spirit-tree destination</strong>; warped-creature tasks can be unlocked later. Neither a warped sceptre nor any other drop is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Path_of_Glouphrie#Rewards" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Verified rewards</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-slayer-58" number="6" title="Finish only the live Slayer remainder to actual 58">
        <p>Read Slayer XP <strong>after using Path's 20,000-XP lamp</strong>. An account entering Path at the exact level-56 floor of <strong>184,040 XP</strong> emerges with at least <strong>204,040 XP</strong>; level 57 begins at 203,254 and level 58 at 224,466. That exact-floor case needs at most <strong>20,426 more Slayer XP</strong>, but your live gap is likely different. Resume ordinary tasks, then <strong>stop at actual 58</strong>. This makes real progress toward the eventual Quest Cape 74-Slayer gate and opens Cave Horrors; it is not a reason to train straight to 60, 69 or 74 here.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i31-black-mask" title="Black mask — recommended, optional and resumable" optional={true}>
        <p>At actual 58 Slayer with Cabin Fever complete, you <em>may</em> try for a black mask from <strong>Cave Horrors</strong> (about <strong>1/512</strong> per kill). The mask's on-task melee accuracy/damage bonus and later Slayer-helmet use make it valuable during the eventual 58→74 journey, but <strong>the Quest Cape / Fire Cape route does not wait here for the drop</strong>. Do one bounded session if you want the upgrade. If it drops, great; otherwise leave and return in a future Slayer mood. No kill count, helmet unlock or Slayer-point purchase is mandatory. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Killing_cave_horror" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cave Horror reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>First trip:</strong> take Bill Teach's boat from Port Phasmatys to Mos Le'Harmless, then run east to the Mos Le'Harmless Cave. Bring a <strong>lit light source and witchwood icon</strong> (buy the icon from a Slayer master if absent); keep the icon equipped until you have other valid scream protection. Use ordinary melee gear, food and Prayer as needed; Cave Horrors' attacks can hurt through unsuitable melee armour, so a modest Ranged/dragonhide setup or the entrance safespot is also fine. Bank useful herbs/seeds, nature runes and alchable equipment; leave junk. Stop whenever the session ceases to be fun.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Magic · last small gate</div><h2>Apply Path's Magic XP before choosing a method.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-magic-67" number="7" title="Reach actual 67 Magic, and no higher target yet">
        <p>Read live Magic XP <strong>after Path's 5,000-XP lamp</strong>. The conservative Chapter 2 floor of <strong>514,111 XP</strong> becomes <strong>519,111 XP</strong>; level 67 begins at <strong>547,953 XP</strong>. So the maximum conservative remainder is <strong>28,842 XP</strong>. You may need much less, or already be 67. The bounded High Level Alchemy estimate is <code>ceil((547953 - current Magic XP) / 65)</code> casts—at the exact floor, about <strong>444 casts</strong>. High Alchemy requires the <strong>standard spellbook</strong>; use banked sensible profitable/break-even alchables and nature runes if convenient, but do not manufacture 444 specific items just to satisfy this example.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i31-magic-methods" skill="Magic" target="actual 67" why="WGS consumes the live 67 gate; no 75-Magic or barrage target belongs here." recommended="High Alchemy existing useful alchables in bounded batches, if nature runes and the standard spellbook are convenient." relaxed="Cast ordinary combat Magic on a low-risk target or a suitable Slayer task; the upgraded Iban's staff remains available." informational={true} />
        <p>No Mage Training Arena reward grind is needed. <strong>Stop at actual 67 Magic</strong>; Magic 75 belongs beside later Dragon Slayer II/Desert Treasure II requirements.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Grandmaster finale</div><h2>Bank by phase; then solve the fights deliberately.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i31-wgs" number="8" title="Complete While Guthix Sleeps and claim its permanent rewards">
        <p><strong>Hard-check the quest journal and live skill tab before Ivy Sophista in Taverley.</strong> Required quests: The Path of Glouphrie, Defender of Varrock, Fight Arena, Dream Mentor, The Hand in the Sand, Wanted!, Temple of the Eye (including Enter the Abyss), Tears of Guthix, Nature Spirit and A Tail of Two Cats; also <strong>180+ quest points</strong> and Warriors' Guild access. Check actual <strong>72 Thieving, 67 Magic, 66 Agility, 65 Farming, 65 Herblore and 62 Hunter</strong>; the sapphire lantern's Firemaking gate is covered by the route's actual <strong>49+ Firemaking</strong>. Warriors' Guild access uses the existing <strong>Attack + Strength ≥130</strong> (or a single 99), <em>not</em> an Attack/Strength-99 grind. The Chapter 2 audit supplies every gate except Path and the live Magic-67 bridge. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Update%3AWhile_Guthix_Sleeps#Requirements" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex's WGS requirement announcement</a> and <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current detailed quest guide</a>.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Long quest, multiple banks:</strong> stage a small bank pile rather than carry everything at once. The route below groups the unusual items and spells by phase. Rebank before the Black Knight/Surok sequence and again before the Balance Elemental; Quest Helper can supply exact puzzle clicks, but it does not replace the supplies or spellbook checks here.</div>
        <ExpandableNote title="Full WGS bank audit before departure" label="Quest item checklist">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Identity/infiltration:</strong> ring of charos(a) <em>or 500 coins</em>, knife, bronze med helm, iron chainbody, combat gear, food and travel teleports.</li>
            <li><strong>Investigation/serum:</strong> one ordinary log (not redwood), lantern lens, 20 coins for pink dye if not banked, snapdragon seed (Thaerisk can supply one), seed dibber unless Barbarian Farming covers it, charcoal and papyrus (available during the quest).</li>
            <li><strong>Infiltration/temple:</strong> unpowered orb, lit sapphire lantern, Mort myre fungus, restore/stat-recovery supplies and free inventory spaces. Some are obtainable during the quest; bank-check rather than assuming a random stock.</li>
            <li><strong>Spell supplies:</strong> Lunar Astral Contact four times = <strong>8 air + 4 astral + 4 cosmic runes</strong>; a standard-spellbook Charge Orb = <strong>30 of its chosen elemental rune + 3 cosmic</strong>; additional runes for standard elemental attacks, binding, weakening, Telekinetic Grab and alchemy. Keep at least one each of air, water, earth, fire, mind, law and death for quest puzzles, with extra casts' worth where noted below.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These are a <em>bank audit</em>, not a single inventory. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">live quick guide</a> gives exact phase handoffs and obtainable-item locations.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p><strong>Investigation and alliance:</strong> begin with Ivy in Taverley, investigate Movario, then work with Thaerisk at the White Knights' Castle. Carry the ring/coin alternative, log and knife when the investigation calls for them; bring the lens, dye money, seed and dibber for the serum phase. Thaerisk can give a snapdragon seed. To recruit the four Slayer heroes efficiently, use the <strong>Lunar spell Astral Contact</strong> (67 Magic, astral runes) four times; Cyrisus must be contacted magically, while the others can be visited if you prefer. The spell was formerly called <em>NPC Contact</em>; older quest guides may still use that name. Bring the 8 air, 4 astral and 4 cosmic runes, then bank/regear after the alliance phase. The route already owns Lunar access; no new spellbook unlock is needed. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#Amassing_the_masters" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Alliance phase</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Astral_Contact" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current spell name</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Dark Squall and Surok:</strong> switch to the <strong>standard spellbook</strong> before the rune puzzles and Surok fight. Take bronze med helm, iron chainbody, unpowered orb, 30 runes of a chosen Charge Orb element plus 3 cosmic, and <strong>nine free inventory spaces</strong> for the infiltration. Do not rely on a powered staff for puzzle casts or for damaging Surok; he is immune to powered-staff damage. For Surok, pack actual runes for <strong>all four elemental attack spells</strong>, a bind (Snare/Entangle), a weakening spell (Weaken/Enfeeble), <strong>Telekinetic Grab</strong> and <strong>Low/High Alchemy</strong>: that means appropriate air/water/earth/fire plus mind/chaos/death as your chosen attacks require, body/soul for the chosen debuff, nature for alchemy and law for Telekinetic Grab. Recheck spellbook/rune pouch before entering. Bind his fast melee minion, weaken the strong one, telegrab then alch the explosive orb, and counter his elemental surges with the opposite element (fire with water, water with fire, air with earth, earth with air). Bring food and Prayers for the hostile knights and Surok; bank afterward. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current spell and puzzle sequence</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Chasm and temple:</strong> take the Dark Squall disguise when asked, a <strong>lit sapphire lantern</strong> for the Tears of Guthix chasm, Prayer points for Bloom, and fungus/druid-pouch and other puzzle supplies as the quest requests. Leave roughly seven free inventory slots; a spade, hammer and chisel can be obtained in the chasm. A games necklace reaches Tears of Guthix; climb down using the lantern/light creature route. Rebank after opening the temple's final door. Do not carry the whole investigation inventory into the boss room.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Balance Elemental—three styles, not two.</strong> Bring your existing dragon scimitar/defender melee setup, a real banked Ranged weapon and ammunition (Ava's accumulator and your best appropriate bow or crossbow), and a Magic weapon/spell such as upgraded Iban's staff with its runes. Add <strong>several super-restore doses, strong food, a lit sapphire lantern and a non-rune emergency teleport</strong> such as an equipped teleport item; Magic can be drained to 1. A Menaphite remedy is helpful if already available, not a new mandatory potion grind. No Bowfa, blowpipe, black mask, Slayer helmet, Fire Cape, brews, Rigour or 90+ combats are assumed. The Elemental uses orange/fire <strong>Ranged</strong>, white/air <strong>Melee</strong> and blue/water <strong>Magic</strong>. Switch the matching protection prayer <em>as its appearance changes, before its next attack animation</em>; then switch your damage style to one it is not protecting against. It begins using protection prayers below half HP; late in the fight it protects against <strong>two styles at once</strong> and attacks faster, so a third damage style is required. Restore drained stats and Prayer, and use the <strong>Stone/pillars to break contact and slow the fight</strong> when overwhelmed: defensive prayer first, damage-style switch second. This is a mechanics check, not a DPS race. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#Balancing_act" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current Balance Elemental mechanics</a>.</div>
        <p><strong>Quest Tormented Demons:</strong> after the Elemental, touch the <strong>Stone of Jas</strong>; it temporarily boosts your combat stats to <strong>255</strong> for the two quest demons. This is explicitly <em>not</em> a reason to pre-grind combat. Fight one at a time, keep the relevant protection prayer up, change your attack style around their protection prayers and move from targeted fire tiles. The Guardians of Armadyl assist. If supplies are low, teleport out and restock; the quest resumes at the demon phase without repeating the Elemental. A cautious player can hide behind the south-western column and let the Guardians do much of the work, but allow time and avoid idle logout. This is the <em>boosted quest encounter</em>, not normal post-quest Tormented Demon farming. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/While_Guthix_Sleeps#The_Stone_of_Jas" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Stone and demon phase</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Death risk:</strong> these are dangerous quest fights, not safe minigame deaths; Hardcore status is at stake. A Balance Elemental death places a grave <strong>by Movario and Darve in the Chasm of Tears</strong>, outside the boss area. You do not need another sapphire lantern merely to retrieve that grave, but you do need one to descend again afterward. Recover items before taking another risk. The south-west column is a quest-demon tactic, not a guaranteed safe spot for normal post-quest Tormented Demons. Teleporting out to bank is safer than pressing onward with exhausted supplies.</p>
        <p>Finish the dialogue and claim <strong>5 quest points; 80,000 Thieving, 75,000 Farming, 75,000 Herblore and 50,000 Hunter XP</strong>; and access to the <strong>Ancient Guthixian Temple and normal Tormented Demons</strong>. Afterward, speak to <strong>Kuradal in Shilo Village</strong> for <strong>Duradel's notes</strong>: their one-time Slayer XP is <strong>15 × your current Slayer level</strong> and they unlock the demonbane-weapon crafting path if a future synapse is obtained. Claim/use the notes when convenient—do not wait dozens of levels to squeeze out a few hundred XP—and record live Slayer XP. A <strong>tormented synapse</strong> (for a future Scorching bow, Emberlight or Purging staff) is a recommended/Endgame gear branch, <strong>not</strong> a required WGS follow-up. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Update%3AWhile_Guthix_Sleeps#Quest_Rewards" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Jagex rewards</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Kuradal" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Kuradal's notes</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.1 complete · mandatory exit only</div>
        <h3>The quest route moves forward; the drop hunt can wait.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests:</strong> Rum Deal, Cabin Fever, The Great Brain Robbery, The Path of Glouphrie and While Guthix Sleeps complete; <strong>Holy wrench retained</strong> and Brain Robbery's 5,000-XP lamp assigned to Slayer.</li>
          <li><strong>Actual levels:</strong> at least <strong>60 Strength, 58 Slayer and 67 Magic</strong>, checked from the live skill tab.</li>
          <li><strong>Access and rewards:</strong> Mos Le'Harmless/Cave Horrors, Poison Waste Dungeon/spirit-tree destination, Ancient Guthixian Temple/normal Tormented Demons, all four Path lamps and WGS's large Thieving/Farming/Herblore/Hunter rewards claimed. Speak to Kuradal for Duradel's notes when convenient.</li>
          <li><strong>Not guaranteed:</strong> black mask, Slayer helmet, tormented synapse, any demonbane weapon, Bowfa, crystal armour, Fire Cape, rune crossbow or ornate POH. None is silently required by this page's progress meter.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
